WEBVTT

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.570
They did it!

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.080
There's one Gatchaman,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.660
Ninomiya Rui-san, and someone 
we believe to be tied to VAPE.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.880
The Gatchaman has reached 
the top of a skyscraper in Shibuya!

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.250
<b>Urgent News: Mr. Ninomiya Rui Bleeding! 
 Gatchaman vs. VAPE</b>

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.450
We have reports that it's the 
rookie, Misudachi Tsubasa-chan!

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.310
<i>Go, Tsubasa-chan!</i>

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.310
So he's their leader.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.560
Cherry Blossom Vine!

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.100
Rui-senpai!

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.270
Out of the way!

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.650
Innocent Storm!

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.590
<i>Oh! Who's that now?</i>

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.980
<i>Is he a new Gatchaman, too?</i>

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.000
<i>He's tearing through the red CROWDS!</i>

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.900
Innocent Storm!

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:37.670
Gel-chan!

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.550
Let's save Rui-kun together!

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:40.690
Thank you!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.210
<i>Go, Gatchaman!</i>

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.600
They're so cool!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.320
Just look at their teamwork!

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.310
Nice!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.020
<b>Urgent News: The New Gatchaman is on a Roll! 
Gatchaman vs. VAPE</b>

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.200
<i>Go!</i>

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.170
<i>Good job, team!</i>

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.200
<i>Go!</i>

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.170
Why can't they all get along?

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.740
Get 'em!

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.140
I surrender.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.920
My purpose has been more than met.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.010
VAPE has lost!

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:26.520
The leader's been captured!

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.520
You lost!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.840
Die, VAPE!

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.010
Get out of here!

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.320
<i>Thanks to valiant action from one 
of our commentators, Tsubasa-chan,</i>

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.020
<i>it appears the matter's been resolved!</i>

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:43.450
<b>Urgent News: VAPE Leader Arrested! 
 Cowardly Terrorist Attack on Shibuya Quelled!</b>

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.970
<i>We did it, everyone!</i>

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.400
<i>The VAPE leader has been 
captured by Gatchaman!</i>

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.900
Yeah!

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.900
Nice.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.260
Shh!

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.620
Quiet, please.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.090
Sorry!

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.330
<i>And it seems Ninomiya Rui-san is alive.</i>

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.500
Rui-kun!

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.500
Rui-senpai, everything's going to be all right.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.250
We caught the VAPE leader!

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.340
Why...

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.000
Why did you... interfere?

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:09.850
Interfere?

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.540
I told you...

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.270
not to come.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.520
What?!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.480
How could I just do nothing?!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:18.860
Rui-senpai?!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.790
How is he, Utsutsu-chan?

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.700
Don't worry.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.130
I won't let him die!

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.560
I saved him,

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.970
but he said I interfered.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.860
Why'd he say that?

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.670
Looks like it all worked out in the end!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.390
This road is temporarily closed

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.930
in order to remove debris.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.690
It's not safe.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.970
Please stay back.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:54.480
Hang in there.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:55.520
Hang in there...

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.940
<i>We'll be broadcasting live from 
the Prime Minister's residence</i>

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.490
<i>about the CROWDS upheaval in Shibuya.</i>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.890
This is so sad.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:06.630
This planet's in more 
disarray than I'd thought.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.950
There'd be no conflict 
if everyone becomes united.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.970
Is conflict so bad?

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:12.690
What?

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.460
What are you saying, Senpai?

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.290
Of course it's bad!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.470
Isn't it sometimes necessary?

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.680
Are you saying it's okay 
for people to get hurt?

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.750
No, but when people aren't united,

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.080
there can be pretty sparkles when they clash!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.370
Huh?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.760
I don't really get what you mean.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.110
Don't mind her.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.900
She sometimes says stuff that makes no sense.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.150
It does make sense!

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:38.940
By the way, newbie.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.430
I believe I told you to be on standby.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:44.180
You shouldn't disobey orders.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.080
I apologize for not following orders.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.850
But I don't think I did anything wrong!

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:50.130
What?!

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.910
I couldn't let Rui-senpai die!

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.950
There's nothing more important than life!

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.780
Is that true?

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.350
Huh?

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.890
Is there nothing more important than life?

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:01.100
Of course not!

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.710
Heroes should protect life above all else!

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:07.080
But you don't know if Rui-kun thinks that.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:10.890
Then are you saying I should've 
just let Rui-senpai die?

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.610
That's not what I mean,

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:16.420
but I think it would've been 
okay to give Rui-kun more time.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.330
But Rui-senpai was hurt really bad!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.350
I couldn't just watch and do nothing!

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:22.900
You've said things like 
how conflict's necessary

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.630
and how Rui-senpai shouldn't 
have been helped.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.050
You're cold, Hajime-senpai.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:28.650
Am I?

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:29.950
Am I cold?

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.350
"There's nothing more important than life."

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.070
That's a good motto for the Gatchaman. 
We're supposed to love peace.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:37.220
But you shouldn't disobey orders.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.960
Heroes need to be flexible.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.210
It's a matter of degree.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:46.550
Hey, the newbie is learning 
all this from watching you.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:50.300
<i>Prime Minister Sugayama has begun 
an emergency press conference.</i>

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.300
<i>We're broadcasting live from 
the prime minister's residence.</i>

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:57.310
Regarding the red CROWDS disturbance 
in Shibuya earlier today,

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.640
we have something to share with our citizens.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.800
The red CROWDS, controlled by 
the criminal organization VAPE,

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:08.300
were the sole perpetrators 
in the terrorist incident

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.020
targeting the Prime Minister's plane.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:12.660
We arrested the leader 
of that organization today.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:16.550
CROWDS have made major 
contributions to various sectors

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:19.390
in terms of labor, medical assistance, 
and social work.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:24.460
I would like to support CROWDS' 
continued presence in our society.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.020
This is Smile TV.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:27.120
So are you saying that the blue CROWDS

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.220
would never instigate a similar 
incident in the future?

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:35.300
The blue CROWDS are under 
X's absolute supervision.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.310
They would never give rise to similar violence.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.350
<i>I'm your proof.</i>

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.600
<i>Just look at me.</i>

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:47.230
<i>Who can say that 
Ninomiya Rui, who oversees X,</i>

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.520
<i>won't end up like me?</i>

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:00.880
CROWDS have made major contributions 
to various sectors...

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.550
<i>CROWDS scary!</i>

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:05.670
I would like to support CROWDS' 
continued presence in our society.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.750
<i>I can't trust the blues anymore, either!</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.670
<i>Do we really need CROWDS?</i>

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:09.100
<i>The Millione Show!</i>

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:10.960
<i>Hello. In today's Millione Show, 
we'll start with this topic:</i>

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.690
<i>CROWDS terrorism in Shibuya!</i>

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.260
<i>The new Gatchaman and 
a mysterious hero save the day!</i>

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.370
<i>I see!</i>

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.860
<i>So the mysterious hero who 
fought alongside Tsubasa-chan</i>

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.640
<i>was Gelsadra-kun!</i>

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.060
Yes, that's right.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.700
I have to thank you for all of Japan.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.520
Thanks to you, the terrorists were quelled,

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.990
and Suzuki Rizumu, who's suspected 
of being their leader, was arrested.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.070
Tsubasa-chan and Gelsadra-kun,

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.280
you're both new heroes who'll protect Japan.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:37.930
Thank you!

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.650
I'll continue to do my best!

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:45.060
We've received a ton of questions about 
you two ever since our broadcast yesterday.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:48.300
You're viewed favorably on-line, too.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.880
This must mean that our citizens 
have acknowledged your worth.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:55.340
I just wanted to take 
everyone's sadness away.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.090
You're so modest!

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.320
So, what's become a prominent issue is this!

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:01.810
<b>Urgent Debate: Are CROWDS Safe? 
 Can We Trust the Blue CROWDS?!</b>

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.330
We now know that once 
CROWDS get out of control,

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:08.020
they can cause incidents of this magnitude.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:12.230
Don't you think this strikes 
some fear into people's hearts?

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:13.440
Huh?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.600
Wait a minute,

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.710
the ones behind the incident 
are the red CROWDS.

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:18.950
They're different from 
the blue CROWDS, you know.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.060
Sure, that's what Prime 
Minister Sugayama said, too.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.740
But we're discussing whether 
the CROWDS are as safe

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.660
as the Prime Minister says they are.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:27.620
What do you two think?

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.820
I think they are dangerous.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:32.240
If this is what can happen,

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:35.460
why push to keep using CROWDS?

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:36.660
Yeah.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.890
I don't want scary things 
like that to happen again.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.890
This terrorist attack wouldn't 
have happened in the first place

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.770
if there had been no CROWDS.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:46.000
So there's rising criticism

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.050
of Prime Minister Sugayama for carelessly 
pushing the adoption of CROWDS,

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:52.270
and of Mr. Ninomiya Rui for developing them.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.900
Mr. Ninomiya Rui has been critically 
injured during the attack.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.620
He's currently hospitalized,

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.570
but everyone's waiting to hear what 
he has to say after he recovers.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:05.940
Hang in there...

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:07.830
Hang in there.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.100
What Rui-rui did was suicide.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.210
You should've just let him die.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.980
Saying stuff like "I believe," like whatever.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:18.090
You know why, Katze-san.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:20.470
You know why Rui-kun did that.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.470
Huh?

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.480
No way!

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:24.040
No clue!

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.840
He's just an idiot!

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:27.480
Lololol!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:32.230
I'd like to unite everyone's hearts 
and get rid of all conflict.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.380
Yeah, I think that's a great idea.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:37.450
Hajime-senpai said a lot of things,

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:40.310
but it's just sad when 
people hurt each other.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:42.160
Yeah.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.420
That's why I want to know 
what everyone thinks.

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:54.120
You can really know that?

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:56.990
Yep.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.170
I got it!

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.640
Maybe it's time to cut OD from the show.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:03.970
<b>Toriyama Millio-sama</b>

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.970
Oh, why?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:08.390
Our ratings have shot up after 
OD-san became a regular.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.660
I'm talking about the future of the show.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.250
If a... <i>supporter</i> is a program regular,

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:16.070
we might make a negative impression 
on our viewers, you know?

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.320
I see. You're right.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.500
Look ahead, will you?

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:21.410
If you don't,

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.430
we'd risk losing our longtime hold 
on the top spot in our airtime.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.250
Come in.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:31.560
Oh! Gel-chan, Tsubasa-chan!

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.100
Thanks for coming today.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.360
You two are so popular!

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.180
Please become our regulars!

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:40.600
Millio-san, I want you 
to unite everyone's hearts.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:41.430
Huh?

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.360
Everyone listens to what you have to say.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:47.270
I think you'd be capable 
of uniting everyone's hearts

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:50.340
and creating a world without conflict.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:52.680
What are you talking about, Gel-chan?

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:55.520
You shouldn't ask Millio-san 
to do something like that!

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.520
Why not?

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:57.940
It's what everyone wants.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:01.530
They want a world without conflict, 
where no one is sad.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:05.120
You say really interesting things!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.170
But I don't think I can.

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:08.950
I'm not cut out for the job.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.280
Being the host of a daytime 
TV show is the best I can do.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.470
Really?

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:15.140
I'm sorry, Millio-san!

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:17.960
Gel-chan doesn't know that 
much about Earth yet.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.630
It's okay.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.340
<b>Toriyama Millio-sama</b>

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.340
I don't understand...

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:26.510
Aliens sure are different from us.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:30.020
Right? We should make them regulars.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:33.610
I thought Millio-san could do it, though.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.770
Unite everyone's hearts.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.890
You're still hung up on that?

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.920
You can't ask Millio-san 
to do things like that!

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:43.860
Then who should I ask?

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:46.910
Who?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.050
Um, someone important?

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.540
Who's someone important?

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.040
Well... a politician, maybe?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.520
A politician?

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:55.420
Like Prime Minister Sugayama?

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.380
Guys, we have an emergency!

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.640
Prime Minister Sugayama 
just announced his resignation!

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:05.790
<i>Like I said, I'd like 
to resign as prime minister</i>

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.470
<i>and nominate myself as a candidate for 
the popular Prime Minister election to follow.</i>

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:12.660
<i>I'd like to stake my re-election 
on what all Japanese citizens</i>

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.180
<i>believe the CROWDS to be worth.</i>

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:17.720
<i>If you truly believe CROWDS 
are not necessary in society,</i>

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:19.970
<i>let me lose the election!</i>

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:23.240
I'd like the people to vote!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:30.080
<b>Prime Minister Sugayama Resigns; 
Puts CROWDS to the Popular Vote in the First Prime Minister Elections</b>

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:30.080
<b>Emergency Broadcast</b>

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:27.840
There will be an election to choose the 
next Prime Minister via smart phone vote,

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.080
as stipulated by legislation 
passed last year.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.830
Sugayama-chan is such a man.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.150
What's the prime minister election?

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:38.300
Everyone will vote to decide who'll 
be the leader of the government.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.850
I don't think it's good strategy to put your

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:43.840
own neck on the line based on 
what people think about CROWDS.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:45.580
It isn't?

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:50.000
I don't think it's such a bad idea to put 
the question to a general public vote

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.760
rather than just have CROWDS banned outright.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:54.700
What a backwards planet this is,

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.950
to get in a scuffle about 
something as minor as CROWDS.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:14:00.520
How can children grow up 
in safety on a planet like this?

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:03.920
The danger of CROWDS has become 
known to the world at large.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.220
Suzuki Rizumu did a good job.

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:09.780
No one can feel safe about 
using CROWDS anymore.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.510
I wonder about that.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.460
It's like trying to ban all cars

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.870
just because someone lost 
control of their car.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.860
CROWDS are far more dangerous than cars.

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:23.130
They are tools humanity 
was not prepared to use.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:27.510
Man, this is why this planet will always 
remain under protective surveillance.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:31.430
There are people who are putting 
it to good use to help others.

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:34.350
It's the rule of 2:6:2.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.530
You're talking about how 
in a group of people,

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.250
20% will be intelligent,

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.690
60% will be average,

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.650
and 20% will be foolish 
as a general rule, right?

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:46.660
Right now, only 20% are able 
to use CROWDS as intended.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:49.690
When the average 60% becomes capable 
of using CROWDS at that level,

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:51.980
that's when we can say CROWDS 
are being used as intended.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:55.220
But it's quite possible 
that CROWDS will become

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:59.050
a destructive force in society 
before that ever happens.

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:00.000
Um!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.650
Am I part of the 20% or the 60%?

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:06.580
You're talking all high and mighty like that,

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.970
but is it that fun to look down on 
people and classify them that way?

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.720
No, Tsubasa-chan, it's not about having fun.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.440
Is this something we Gatchaman 
should be even talking about?

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:18.810
We're heroes,

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:22.980
so isn't it more important that 
we focus on helping people in need?

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.420
Well said, Tsubasa-chan.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:28.240
This is what I meant by 
clashing and sparkles!

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:29.600
Huh?

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:33.410
Lately, people are all "meh,"

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:37.460
but you're "bam!" You know?

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:41.780
That's why we need you right now.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.490
I don't really understand what you mean,

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:46.630
but is this what we should 
be really thinking about?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:49.540
I don't know if we should be,

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:51.300
but I find myself thinking about it!

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.000
Yes, hello?

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.520
No, it's fine.

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:02.130
Okay, I'll go over when I can.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:05.310
Leader, may I go somewhere for a bit?

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:07.180
Hm?

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:08.960
Well, we finished our debrief,

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.940
and we have no particular 
plan to sortie at the moment.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.870
You have my permission.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:14.320
Thank you! Excuse me!

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:20.670
Where are you going, Tsubasa-chan?

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.680
Nowhere special. Want to come?

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:24.170
Yeah.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:28.870
I got to know some of the

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:31.590
neighborhood association people 
yesterday after the attack.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:35.000
They said they were going to be clearing 
debris today, so I thought I'd chip in.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:35.890
Great!

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.350
I'll help, too!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.480
Oh, Tsubasa-chan!

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:42.230
Hi, everyone!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.700
You must be Gel-chan.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.060
Thanks, you two! What a big help.

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:49.820
C'mon, guys! We have friends!

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:53.060
You should've invited 
Hajime-chan and the others, too.

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:55.510
It'd get done faster if everyone chipped in.

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:59.280
I just thought they might say it's 
not something Gatchaman should do.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:01.830
Everyone's thinking too much.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.310
Yeah, you're right!

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:06.740
Why do heroes need to think about 2s and 6s

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Authorized 
Personnel 
Only</b>

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:08.240
and categorize people into groups?

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:09.840
I don't like it.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.300
If everyone united their hearts 
and tackled problems together,

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.550
they'd be able to solve anything.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:16.820
You're exactly right!

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.560
I get what you're saying 
so much more than the others.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.840
Tsubasa-chan, who are you voting for?

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:22.840
Huh?

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:25.080
Oh, you mean for the 
prime minister elections?

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.820
Wouldn't you end up voting for Sugayama?

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.700
You think so?

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:30.400
What do you think, Tsubasa-chan?

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:34.030
I know it's not the best way to go about it,

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:36.110
but I don't really understand 
the whole process,

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.120
so I'll just take a quick 
look at election time

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.960
and vote for the one who looks good to me.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.150
I guess it's like that.

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.700
It doesn't seem to matter who you vote for.

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:49.000
Maybe Sugayama's just the safe choice.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:56.430
The Millione Show...

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.010
<b>Info-Live: The Millione Show</b>

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:06.060
Today, we have our semi-regulars, 
Sadra-kun and Tsubasa-chan, with us!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.690
Isn't it time you became real regulars?

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:12.520
Well, here's the first piece of news today!

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:16.740
<b>Prime Minister Sugayama Resigns! 
 The First Popular Prime Minister Election Coming Up!</b>

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:17.450
The first popular Prime Minister 
elections will soon be held,

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:26.240
<b>What Is the Popular Prime Minister Election? 
Prime Minister Resigns -> Smart Phone Vote</b>

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:21.470
but it's to be a smart phone vote.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:24.870
Until now, Japan has been 
an indirect democracy

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.160
where the most powerful man in government

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:36.010
<b>Appointment by Diet Members -> Election by Japanese Citizens</b>

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:30.050
would be appointed by 
diet members we'd voted in.

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:33.400
But now, Japanese citizens 
can vote for one themselves

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:35.750
with a tap on their smart phones!

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:39.920
Furthermore, there are no age or 
nationality restrictions on candidates!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:40.460
<b>No Age/Nationality Restrictions for Candidates 
Anyone can Nominate Themselves!</b>

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:40.460
<b>Anyone Can Register via smart phone</b>

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.740
That's right!

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:45.040
By law, anyone... babies, grandpas, grandmas,

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:50.480
and even cat station masters and 
aliens can become candidates!

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.020
Ha! He's dreaming.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:56.300
As if an alien could be 
voted in as prime minister.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.860
You think so?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.450
Of course!

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.750
An alien!

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:02.480
An alien prime minister!

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.500
Impossible!

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:04.470
Ridiculous!

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.870
Is it really?

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:10.780
Umm... So the prime minister 
is the top leader of Japan?

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.900
That's right, Gel-chan.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.640
It's an oversimplification,

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:18.530
but the prime minister basically gets 
final say on what happens to Japan.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:22.010
Can that person make 
people's wishes come true?

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:23.430
Yeah.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.330
They're the top gun of democracy,

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:28.520
so you could say that's their role.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.810
Can that person stop everyone's conflict?

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:34.540
I'm sure they could.

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:37.440
Can that person put an end to sadness?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.710
You're asking really tough questions.

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:46.450
Well, I guess the Prime Minister has the 
most power to resolve everyone's problems.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.270
Then I'll run in the 
prime minister elections!

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.440
Huh?

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.510
That's way too fun!

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.250
Hmm... It may not be a bad idea!

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.730
Way fun!

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:02.180
But I don't think you can win.

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:04.800
Is that because I'm an alien?

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.800
No, because you're still a child.

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:08.890
Aliens would be fun.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:13.380
But no one would think 
that a child could do politics.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:16.800
Gel-chan?

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:20.960
What a shock!

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:22.740
That's growing up way too much!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.210
How's this?

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:24.560
Great!

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:26.980
Super great!

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:26.980
Yes, wonderful!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.450
Thumbs up!

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:30.120
Impossible!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.370
An alien as a prime minister candidate?!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:35.030
No way! It's not possible!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.880
Gel-chan's transformed again.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:42.680
I don't think he needs 
to change so many times, though.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:44.130
Tsubasa-chan!

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.040
Y-Yes?

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:49.310
I want you to help me.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.020
What?!

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:55.190
I think we can work together 
to unite everyone's hearts.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.870
Oh, okay! I'll help!

00:20:58.710 --> 00:20:59.910
Yay!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.700
Hey, Gel-chan!

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:06.050
Hajime-tan! He's gonna be a huge problem!

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:07.730
If you don't stop him now,

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:09.310
I'm gonna be in a huge pickle!

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:10.790
Help me, Hajime-tan!

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.510
Let's off him!

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:14.770
Let's off Sadra!

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:14.770
I'm gonna sleep.

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:18.090
Hey, don't ignore me.

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:22.020
Talk to me, you worthless bitch! Bitch! Bitch!

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:24.590
You shitty bitch!

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:26.840
Here!

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.900
If you tap that "yes,"

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:31.850
<b>The First Popular Prime Minister Elections 
 Do you nominate yourself?</b>

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:30.950
you become a candidate?

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:31.850
That's right.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:33.310
Here, Gel-chan.

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:36.540
Do you wish to nominate 
yourself as a candidate?

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:38.060
Yes!

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.490
Your application has been accepted.
